1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,440
When we talk about what makes somebody male or female,

2
00:00:03,860 --> 00:00:06,920
it sounds like it's very simple, you're either male or female,

3
00:00:07,260 --> 00:00:10,180
but when you are figuring out what sex somebody is,

4
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:14,540
you're looking at internal genitalia, external genitalia,

5
00:00:14,700 --> 00:00:18,520
chromosomes, certain genetic mutations, hormones,

6
00:00:18,960 --> 00:00:20,460
there's just a bunch of different things.

7
00:00:21,260 --> 00:00:24,760
And most people, those all line up, and some people, they don't line up.

8
00:00:24,760 --> 00:00:29,680
And you might have most of the characteristics of male,

9
00:00:29,680 --> 00:00:31,280
but some things that are female.

10
00:00:32,060 --> 00:00:35,120
For example, one of them is called congenital androgen insensitivity.

11
00:00:35,660 --> 00:00:38,220
You have a person who is XY.

12
00:00:38,620 --> 00:00:40,240
Every cell in their body is XY.

13
00:00:40,940 --> 00:00:47,060
But the androgen receptor, the protein that detects the testosterone, doesn't work.

14
00:00:47,660 --> 00:00:50,300
So this is a person, every cell in their body is XY.

15
00:00:50,540 --> 00:00:52,520
They have male levels of testosterone.

16
00:00:52,520 --> 00:00:54,060
They look completely female.

17
00:00:55,940 --> 00:00:59,600
These people don't get diagnosed until puberty when they don't have a period.

18
00:00:59,680 --> 00:01:01,600
Because they have internal testes.

19
00:01:01,660 --> 00:01:02,680
They don't have any ovaries.

20
00:01:03,100 --> 00:01:04,420
They don't develop a uterus or a vagina.

21
00:01:04,420 --> 00:01:04,540
You know?

22
00:01:04,540 --> 00:01:34,520
Thank you.

